IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 29A to 31: national units of measurement, service of notices, electronic service of infringement notices, public notices and advertising.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- The counting of time in ss 29 and 30(1), (2) is in tas-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `s 29A: application of national standards of weights and measures`

-- src:611 | (1) On and after the date from which, by virtue of the operation of the Commonwealth Act, the Commonwealth legal units of measurement of a physical quantity are the sole legal units of measurement of that physical quantity, a reference in any Act to a unit of measurement of that physical quantity shall, if there is a Commonwealth legal unit of measurement of that physical quantity of the same name and unless the contrary intention appears, be read as a reference to that Commonwealth legal unit of measurement.
@ref s 29A(1) (src:611)
GIVEN `the day the Commonwealth legal units of measurement of the physical quantity became the sole legal units of measurement of it` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `there is a Commonwealth legal unit of measurement of that physical quantity of the same name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(1): a reference in an Act to a unit of measurement is read as a reference to the Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` `the day the Commonwealth legal units of measurement of the physical quantity became the sole legal units of measurement of it` `the day in question` `there is a Commonwealth legal unit of measurement of that physical quantity of the same name` `the contrary intention appears` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the Commonwealth legal units of measurement of the physical quantity became the sole legal units of measurement of it`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST soleFrom THEN
        BRANCH IF `the day in question` BELOW soleFrom THEN JUST FALSE   -- "On and after the date": before it is outside the period
               IF NOT (`there is a Commonwealth legal unit of measurement of that physical quantity of the same name`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- the text says "if there is"
               IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:615 | Commonwealth Act means the National Measurement Act 1960 of the Commonwealth, and includes that Act as amended from time to time and any Commonwealth Act passed in substitution for that Act;
@ref s 29A(2) Commonwealth Act (src:615)
GIVEN title IS A STRING
      `it is an amendment of the National Measurement Act 1960 of the Commonwealth, or a Commonwealth Act passed in substitution for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(2): the Act is the Commonwealth Act` title `it is an amendment of the National Measurement Act 1960 of the Commonwealth, or a Commonwealth Act passed in substitution for it` MEANS
    IF title EQUALS "National Measurement Act 1960" OR `it is an amendment of the National Measurement Act 1960 of the Commonwealth, or a Commonwealth Act passed in substitution for it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:617 | Commonwealth legal unit of measurement means a unit of measurement prescribed under the Commonwealth Act.
@ref s 29A(2) Commonwealth legal unit of measurement (src:617)
GIVEN `the unit of measurement is prescribed under the Commonwealth Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29A(2): the unit is a Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` `the unit of measurement is prescribed under the Commonwealth Act` MEANS
    `the unit of measurement is prescribed under the Commonwealth Act`

#ASSERT `s 29A(1): a reference in an Act to a unit of measurement is read as a reference to the Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` (JUST (Date 1 7 1990)) (Date 1 7 1990) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(1): a reference in an Act to a unit of measurement is read as a reference to the Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` (JUST (Date 1 7 1990)) (Date 2 7 1990) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(1): a reference in an Act to a unit of measurement is read as a reference to the Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` (JUST (Date 1 7 1990)) (Date 30 6 1990) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29A(1): a reference in an Act to a unit of measurement is read as a reference to the Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` NOTHING (Date 2 7 1990) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29A(1): a reference in an Act to a unit of measurement is read as a reference to the Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` (JUST (Date 1 7 1990)) (Date 2 7 1990) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29A(1): a reference in an Act to a unit of measurement is read as a reference to the Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` (JUST (Date 1 7 1990)) (Date 2 7 1990) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29A(2): the Act is the Commonwealth Act` "National Measurement Act 1960" FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(2): the Act is the Commonwealth Act` "National Measurement Act 2030" TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(2): the Act is the Commonwealth Act` "Trade Practices Act 1974" FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29A(2): the unit is a Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29A(2): the unit is a Commonwealth legal unit of measurement` FALSE)

§ `s 29AB: service of notices and other documents`

DECLARE `Kind of person to be served` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `any other person`

DECLARE `Way of serving a notice or other document` IS ONE OF
    `giving it to the person`
    `leaving it at the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server`
    `sending it by post to the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server`
    `leaving it at the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business`
    `sending it by post to the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business`
    `some other way`

-- src:621 | (1) If an Act authorizes, requires or permits a notice or other document to be served on a person, whether the expression "serve", "deliver", "give" or "send" or any other expression is used, without directing it to be served in a particular manner, the notice or document may be served –
-- src:623 | (a) on a natural person –
-- src:625 | (i) by giving it to the person; or
-- src:627 | (ii) by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server of the notice or other document; or
-- src:629 | (b) on any other person by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business.
@ref s 29AB(1) (src:621-629)
GIVEN `an Act authorizes, requires or permits a notice or other document to be served on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act directs it to be served in a particular manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Kind of person to be served`
      way IS A `Way of serving a notice or other document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` `an Act authorizes, requires or permits a notice or other document to be served on a person` `the Act directs it to be served in a particular manner` person way MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`an Act authorizes, requires or permits a notice or other document to be served on a person`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "If"
           IF `the Act directs it to be served in a particular manner` THEN JUST FALSE   -- the "If" clause ends "without directing it to be served in a particular manner"
           IF person EQUALS `a natural person` AND (way EQUALS `giving it to the person` OR way EQUALS `leaving it at the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server` OR way EQUALS `sending it by post to the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server`) THEN JUST TRUE
           IF person EQUALS `any other person` AND (way EQUALS `leaving it at the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business` OR way EQUALS `sending it by post to the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business`) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:631 | (2) Nothing in subsection (1) –
-- src:633 | (a) affects the operation of any other law that authorizes or requires the service of a notice or document otherwise than as provided by that subsection; or
-- src:635 | (b) affects the power of a court or person acting judicially to authorize service of a notice or document otherwise than as provided in that subsection.
@ref s 29AB(2) (src:631-635)
GIVEN `another law authorizes or requires service otherwise than as provided by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court or person acting judicially has authorized service otherwise than as provided in that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service was effected in the way that other law or authorization provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29AB(2): subsection (1) leaves the service effective` `another law authorizes or requires service otherwise than as provided by subsection (1)` `a court or person acting judicially has authorized service otherwise than as provided in that subsection` `the service was effected in the way that other law or authorization provides` MEANS
    IF (`another law authorizes or requires service otherwise than as provided by subsection (1)` OR `a court or person acting judicially has authorized service otherwise than as provided in that subsection`) AND `the service was effected in the way that other law or authorization provides`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `giving it to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `leaving it at the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `sending it by post to the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `leaving it at the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE FALSE `any other person` `leaving it at the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE FALSE `any other person` `sending it by post to the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE FALSE `any other person` `giving it to the person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `some other way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` TRUE TRUE `a natural person` `giving it to the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` FALSE FALSE `a natural person` `giving it to the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(2): subsection (1) leaves the service effective` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(2): subsection (1) leaves the service effective` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29AB(2): subsection (1) leaves the service effective` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29AB(2): subsection (1) leaves the service effective` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 30(3) and s 30A: addresses for letters, and electronic service of infringement notices`

-- src:649 | (3) Except where otherwise provided any such letter as aforesaid may be addressed to the usual or last known address of the person to whom it is to be sent.
@ref s 30(3) (src:649)
GIVEN `the letter is one to which section 30(1) or (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter is addressed to the usual or last known address of the person to whom it is to be sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3): the letter may be so addressed` `the letter is one to which section 30(1) or (2) applies` `it is otherwise provided` `the letter is addressed to the usual or last known address of the person to whom it is to be sent` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the letter is one to which section 30(1) or (2) applies`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `it is otherwise provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the letter is addressed to the usual or last known address of the person to whom it is to be sent` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:655 | (a) may be served electronically if the intended recipient of the notice consents to such service; and
@ref s 30A(a) (src:655)
GIVEN `the document is an infringement notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intended recipient of the notice consents to service electronically` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30A(a): the infringement notice may be served electronically` `the document is an infringement notice` `the intended recipient of the notice consents to service electronically` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the document is an infringement notice`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           IF `the intended recipient of the notice consents to service electronically` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- the text says "if the intended recipient of the notice consents"

-- src:657 | (b) is taken to have been served on the intended recipient if it is sent electronically to an address or number provided for that purpose.
@ref s 30A(b) (src:657)
GIVEN `the document is an infringement notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent electronically to an address or number provided for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30A(b): the infringement notice is taken to have been served on the intended recipient` `the document is an infringement notice` `it is sent electronically to an address or number provided for that purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the document is an infringement notice`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           IF `it is sent electronically to an address or number provided for that purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- the text says "if it is sent electronically"

#ASSERT `s 30(3): the letter may be so addressed` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(3): the letter may be so addressed` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(3): the letter may be so addressed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30(3): the letter may be so addressed` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30A(a): the infringement notice may be served electronically` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30A(a): the infringement notice may be served electronically` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30A(a): the infringement notice may be served electronically` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30A(b): the infringement notice is taken to have been served on the intended recipient` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30A(b): the infringement notice is taken to have been served on the intended recipient` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30A(b): the infringement notice is taken to have been served on the intended recipient` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 31: public notices and advertising`

DECLARE `Place of publication` IS ONE OF
    `the Gazette`
    `a newspaper`
    `the Gazette and a newspaper`

-- src:661 | (1) Where by any Act it is provided that public notification or notice shall be given of any matter not required by law to be published in full, such provision shall be construed to mean that a notice comprising the essential features of such matter shall be published in the Gazette or in a newspaper, or in both, as may be indicated by the context.
@ref s 31(1) (src:661)
GIVEN `by an Act public notification or notice shall be given of a matter not required by law to be published in full` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place of publication the context indicates` IS A MAYBE (`Place of publication`)
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Place of publication`)
`s 31(1): a notice comprising the essential features of the matter is to be published in` `by an Act public notification or notice shall be given of a matter not required by law to be published in full` `the place of publication the context indicates` MEANS
    IF `by an Act public notification or notice shall be given of a matter not required by law to be published in full`
    THEN `the place of publication the context indicates`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:663 | (2) Where by any Act it is provided that any matter shall be advertised, then, unless the contrary intention appears, such matter shall be published in such publications, if any, as may be specified by such provision, and if no particular publication is specified therein, the same shall be published in a newspaper.
@ref s 31(2) (src:663)
GIVEN `by an Act a matter shall be advertised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publications specified by the provision` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`s 31(2): the matter is to be published in` `by an Act a matter shall be advertised` `the contrary intention appears` `the publications specified by the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`by an Act a matter shall be advertised`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the publications specified by the provision`
               WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST (LIST "a newspaper")
               WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (p FOLLOWED BY rest)

-- src:665 | (3) Where no number of publications is prescribed in any such provision as aforesaid, it shall be sufficient to publish the prescribed matter once in each of the ways prescribed by such provision, or, if no other way is prescribed, in a newspaper.
@ref s 31(3) (src:665)
GIVEN `the number of publications prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of ways of publishing prescribed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 31(3): the number of publications that is sufficient` `the number of publications prescribed` `the number of ways of publishing prescribed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of publications prescribed`
    WHEN JUST n THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN IF `the number of ways of publishing prescribed` AT LEAST 1 THEN JUST `the number of ways of publishing prescribed` ELSE JUST 1

-- src:669 | newspaper shall mean a daily newspaper generally circulating in the district or place to which the matter required to be published relates or in which it arises.
@ref s 31(4) (src:669)
GIVEN `for the purposes of section 31 and of any such provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication is a daily newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication generally circulates in the district or place to which the matter required to be published relates or in which it arises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(4): the publication is a newspaper` `for the purposes of section 31 and of any such provisions` `the publication is a daily newspaper` `the publication generally circulates in the district or place to which the matter required to be published relates or in which it arises` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`for the purposes of section 31 and of any such provisions`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the publication is a daily newspaper` AND `the publication generally circulates in the district or place to which the matter required to be published relates or in which it arises` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 31(1): a notice comprising the essential features of the matter is to be published in` TRUE (JUST `the Gazette`) EQUALS JUST `the Gazette`
#ASSERT `s 31(1): a notice comprising the essential features of the matter is to be published in` TRUE (JUST `a newspaper`) EQUALS JUST `a newspaper`
#ASSERT `s 31(1): a notice comprising the essential features of the matter is to be published in` TRUE (JUST `the Gazette and a newspaper`) EQUALS JUST `the Gazette and a newspaper`
#ASSERT `s 31(1): a notice comprising the essential features of the matter is to be published in` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31(1): a notice comprising the essential features of the matter is to be published in` FALSE (JUST `the Gazette`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31(2): the matter is to be published in` TRUE FALSE (LIST "the Mercury", "the Examiner") EQUALS JUST (LIST "the Mercury", "the Examiner")
#ASSERT `s 31(2): the matter is to be published in` TRUE FALSE (EMPTY) EQUALS JUST (LIST "a newspaper")
#ASSERT `s 31(2): the matter is to be published in` TRUE TRUE (LIST "the Mercury") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31(2): the matter is to be published in` FALSE FALSE (LIST "the Mercury") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31(3): the number of publications that is sufficient` NOTHING 2 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `s 31(3): the number of publications that is sufficient` NOTHING 1 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 31(3): the number of publications that is sufficient` NOTHING 0 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 31(3): the number of publications that is sufficient` (JUST 3) 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31(4): the publication is a newspaper` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 31(4): the publication is a newspaper` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(4): the publication is a newspaper` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(4): the publication is a newspaper` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
